  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "George Coats, a member of the Paisley thread-manufacturing family, enlarged Belleisle mansion in Ayr and improved its gardens. He and his wife, Margaret, maintained its conservatory and collected paintings, ceramics and glass. The family crest carved on the new wing included the anchor associated with Coats thread.\n\nAfter more than a decade at Belleisle, Coats turned towards the Highlands. He leased Glen Tanar before buying it in 1905, establishing a family connection with the Aberdeenshire estate that continued through later generations. His son Thomas inherited the title and estate when Coats died.",
    "html": "<p>George Coats, a member of the Paisley thread-manufacturing family, enlarged Belleisle mansion in Ayr and improved its gardens. He and his wife, Margaret, maintained its conservatory and collected paintings, ceramics and glass. The family crest carved on the new wing included the anchor associated with Coats thread.</p>\r\n<p>After more than a decade at Belleisle, Coats turned towards the Highlands. He leased Glen Tanar before buying it in 1905, establishing a family connection with the Aberdeenshire estate that continued through later generations. His son Thomas inherited the title and estate when Coats died.</p>\r\n",
